{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base and return its string representation.\n    Base must be an integer between 2 and 9 (inclusive).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"x must be an int\")\n    if not isinstance(base, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"base must be an int\")\n    if base < 2 or base > 9:\n        raise ValueError(\"base must be between 2 and 9 (inclusive)\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    negative = x < 0\n    x = -x if negative else x\n\n    digits = []\n    while x:\n        digits.append(str(x % base))\n        x //= base\n\n    result = \"\".join(reversed(digits))\n    return \"-\" + result if negative else result"}
