{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string by shifting each character five positions backward in the lowercase English alphabet.\n    It expects input produced by encode_shift, ensuring proper wrap-around for 'a'-'z'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 's' must be a string.\")\n\n    decoded_chars = []\n    ord_a = ord('a')\n    ord_z = ord('z')\n\n    for ch in s:\n        ord_ch = ord(ch)\n\n        if not (ord_a <= ord_ch <= ord_z):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input string must contain only lowercase ASCII letters ('a'-'z').\")\n\n        # Apply the reverse shift formula: (ord(ch) - 5 - ord('a')) % 26 + ord('a')\n        shifted_value = (ord_ch - ord_a - 5) % 26\n        decoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_value + ord_a))\n\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
