{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two integers a and b, return the even digits between a and b, in ascending order.\n    For example: generate_integers(2, 8) => [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, int) or not isinstance(b, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"a and b must be integers\")\n\n    lo = min(a, b)\n    hi = max(a, b)\n    result = []\n\n    even_digits = [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]\n\n    for digit in even_digits:\n        if lo <= digit <= hi:\n            result.append(digit)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the even single-digits between a and b (inclusive), in ascending order.\n    The order of inputs a and b does not affect the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_digits = [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]\n    lo = min(a, b)\n    hi = max(a, b)\n    return [d for d in even_digits if lo <= d <= hi]"}
